{
  "_comment": [
    "Per-clip corrections, applied on top of the recipes in phonemes.mjs.",
    "A phonics sound is keyed by its sound id, which the review page shows:",
    "'sound|m', 'sound|ay', 'sound|st'. Words and sentences are keyed by",
    "'<kind>|<value>' exactly as the inventory names them.",
    "",
    "holdMs    how long a held sound lasts (hisses, hums, vowels, buzzes);",
    "          for ch and x, the most of the word ending to keep",
    "targetDb  loudness, if one sound sits oddly against the others",
    "carrier   cut the sound from a different word, written in misaki",
    "          phonemes, e.g. \"hˈʌm\" (the renderer checks the spelling)",
    "word      with carrier: the word's ordinary spelling, for the review page",
    "speed     with carrier: say that word a little slower (not below 0.8)",
    "afterMs   stops, glides, blends, j: how much of the vowel after the",
    "          consonant survives before the fade",
    "noiseDb   z, v, voiced th: how loud the hiss is against the voice",
    "pulse     z, v, voiced th: how strongly the hiss throbs with the voice (0-1)",
    "natural   true: keep a hum, vowel or long vowel as long as it was in",
    "          the word, instead of holding it",
    "pitch     'follow': a held sound keeps the small wobbles in pitch of the",
    "          word it came from, instead of an even, flat pitch",
    "",
    "Render, listen on the review page, change a number, render again.",
    "Only the clips whose tuning changed are regenerated:",
    "  npm run voice:render -- --only sound"
  ],
